  "summary": "Software engineer with more than 10 years of experience in the IT industry working on a full stack (from back-end including database design to front-end) who loves software development in general, not just web applications but any kind of software related task such as designing and building desktop or command line applications and scripting for tasks automation.\n\nFollowing is a list of some of my career achievements:\n•\tLed and coordinated integration tests between the Call Center application of HSBC MX and the new telephony system with teams distributed across 5 different countries making possible to release on time the code to production with a good overall quality.\n•\tDesigned and implemented enhancements for the security questions used for authenticating customers at the HSBC MX Call Center application. This served to strengthen the secureness of some of the questions so they couldn't be easily guessed anymore.\n•\tProvided base design for making sure a customer cannot have more than one session active in the Call Center at any given time making the Call Center department able to comply with Mexico's regulation.\n•\tSuccessfully customized global HSBC WebSphere Portal Call Center application for fulfilling HSBC MX business needs. As a result of this project, HSBC MX started demising legacy systems.\n•\tParticipated as part of the HSBC Global Premier team enhancing public web sites for several countries. The achievement of these projects was that functionality and look and feel redesign for web sites of more than 30 different countries was successfully released on time.\n•\tAnalyzed, designed and implemented an in house ERP system for ETESA company allowing ETESA to demise legacy systems.\n•\t Designed and developed a system for centralizing distributed information for Consorcio Peredo making critical information available on a daily basis for business decision making.\n•\tCreation of a blackberry app for the sales force of ETESA increasing their productivity.",
